          {"option_id": "b", "truth": "correct", "derivation": "sqrt(25*a/5)=sqrt(5a); the negative second expression is -sqrt(144*c/2)=-sqrt(72c).", "misconception": null},
          {"option_id": "c", "truth": "correct", "derivation": "(1/2)^2*6x=3x/2 and (2/3)^2*3y=4y/3, with the second minus sign outside.", "misconception": null},
          {"option_id": "d", "truth": "incorrect", "derivation": "The proposed radicands are (1/2)*6x and (2/3)*3y. At x=y=1 they disagree with the originals.", "misconception": "Use the fractional coefficients themselves inside the radical instead of squaring both numerator and denominator."}
        ]
