    {
      "id": "n40-sign-dependent-extraction",
      "source_numbers": ["826"],
      "view": {
        "mode": "multiple",
        "stem": "Assume $a\\geq0$, $y<0$, and $c<0$. Select all statements that hold for every allowed value.",
        "figure_ids": [],
        "options": [
          {"id": "a", "text": "$\\sqrt{7a^2}=a\\sqrt7$ and $\\sqrt{10y^2}=-y\\sqrt{10}$.", "figure_ids": []},
          {"id": "b", "text": "$\\sqrt{7a^2}=a\\sqrt7$ and $\\sqrt{10y^2}=y\\sqrt{10}$.", "figure_ids": []},
          {"id": "c", "text": "$\\sqrt{27c^6}=3c^3\\sqrt3$.", "figure_ids": []},
          {"id": "d", "text": "$\\sqrt{27c^6}=-3c^3\\sqrt3$.", "figure_ids": []}
        ]
      },
      "intent": {
        "task": "Use the given signs to resolve absolute values when extracting even powers.",
        "source_solution": "Full 826 a-f: a sqrt7,-y sqrt10,4x sqrtx,0.1b^2 sqrtb,5a^3 sqrt(2a),-3c^3 sqrt3. Here a>=0,y<0,x>0,b>=0,a>0,c<0 respectively. sqrt(y^2)=|y|=-y and sqrt(c^6)=|c^3|=-c^3.",
        "unit_reason": "The sign-sensitive cases a,b,f belong together because the apparent square factor needs an absolute-value decision. The odd-power cases are handled as a separate group.",
        "concept_blocks": [6],
        "limitations": ["Identity selection does not prove independent extraction or a written absolute-value argument."],
        "figure_observations": []
      },
      "key": {
        "correct": ["a", "d"],
        "rationales": [
          {"option_id": "a", "truth": "correct", "derivation": "a>=0 gives |a|=a, and y<0 gives |y|=-y, so both displayed square roots stay nonnegative.", "misconception": null},
          {"option_id": "b", "truth": "incorrect", "derivation": "y sqrt10 is strictly negative, but sqrt(10y^2) is positive for y<0.", "misconception": "Replace sqrt(y^2) by y instead of |y| while the first nonnegative variable happens not to expose the mistake."},
          {"option_id": "c", "truth": "incorrect", "derivation": "c<0 implies c^3<0, so 3c^3 sqrt3 is negative and cannot equal the arithmetic square root.", "misconception": "Extract sqrt((3c^3)^2) as 3c^3 without its absolute value."},
          {"option_id": "d", "truth": "correct", "derivation": "27c^6=(3c^3)^2*3 and |3c^3|=-3c^3 under c<0.", "misconception": null}
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "n40-odd-power-extraction",
      "source_numbers": ["826"],
      "view": {
