    {
      "id": "n40-lookup-method-comparison",
      "source_numbers": ["829"],
      "view": {
        "mode": "multiple",
        "stem": "Consider two ways to approximate $6\\sqrt{\\frac13}$ using a square-root table: first look up $\\sqrt{0.3333}$ and multiply the reported value by $6$; or first rewrite the expression as one square root and look it up. Without assuming any particular rounded table entries, select all true statements.",
        "figure_ids": [],
        "options": [
          {"id": "a", "text": "The exact expression $6\\sqrt{\\frac13}$ equals $\\sqrt{12}$.", "figure_ids": []},
          {"id": "b", "text": "Before any table rounding, $6\\sqrt{0.3333}$ equals $\\sqrt{12}$.", "figure_ids": []},
          {"id": "c", "text": "Before any table rounding, $6\\sqrt{0.3333}$ is smaller than $\\sqrt{12}$.", "figure_ids": []},
          {"id": "d", "text": "Looking up the rewritten exact radicand avoids replacing $\\frac13$ by $0.3333$ and avoids multiplying the reported root by $6$ afterward.", "figure_ids": []},
          {"id": "e", "text": "The exact expression $6\\sqrt{\\frac13}$ equals $\\sqrt2$.", "figure_ids": []}
        ]
      },
      "intent": {
        "task": "Compare the two original routes by exact coefficient absorption, truncation direction, and work required, without inventing a table cell.",
        "source_solution": "E=6sqrt(1/3)=sqrt12. F=6sqrt0.3333=sqrt11.9988<E before table rounding; E-F=0.0012/(sqrt12+sqrt11.9988), between 0 and 0.0002. Route 2 keeps the radicand exact and avoids a post-lookup multiplication by 6. Actual route-1 sqrt0.3333 and route-2 sqrt12 table outputs are unobserved, including normalization/corrections and the rounded numerical comparison, and remain deferred.",
        "unit_reason": "One multiple question retains the native method/comparison reasoning, not two counterfeit numeric lookup answers.",
        "concept_blocks": [7],
        "limitations": [
          "829.route1: actual table lookup for sqrt0.3333, equivalent normalized argument 33.33, its observed base/correction entries, and multiplication of the reported result by 6 are deferred.",
          "829.route2: actual table lookup for sqrt12 and comparison of the two observed rounded outputs are deferred.",
          "Selection does not demonstrate executing either numerical lookup or writing the exact method comparison.",
          "No comparison of the total errors of the actual rounded table outputs is asserted."
        ],
        "figure_observations": []
      },
      "key": {
        "correct": ["a", "c", "d"],
        "rationales": [
          {"option_id": "a", "truth": "correct", "derivation": "Squaring the coefficient gives 6^2*(1/3)=12; the expression is nonnegative.", "misconception": null},
          {"option_id": "b", "truth": "incorrect", "derivation": "(6sqrt0.3333)^2=36*0.3333=11.9988, not 12.", "misconception": "Treat the four-digit decimal 0.3333 as exactly 1/3 rather than an approximation."},
          {"option_id": "c", "truth": "correct", "derivation": "0.3333<1/3 and the square-root function is strictly increasing on positive numbers; multiplying by 6 preserves <.", "misconception": null},
          {"option_id": "d", "truth": "correct", "derivation": "The exact rewrite gives argument 12 directly. The original first route replaces 1/3 by 0.3333 and explicitly multiplies the reported root by 6.", "misconception": null},
          {"option_id": "e", "truth": "incorrect", "derivation": "2=6*(1/3) uses the coefficient once; the correct radicand is 6^2*(1/3)=12.", "misconception": "Move the coefficient under the root without squaring it."}
        ]
      }
    },
